From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: v8: ppc64 drop the dead extsw. from kPPC_Tst32's immediate form

kPPC_Tst32 is the fused form of Word32And(x, m) compared with zero.  Its
immediate form currently emits

    andi.  r0,rA,UI       CR0 from the 64-bit result
    extsw. r0,r0          CR0 again, from the sign-extended low word
    bc                    on CR0[EQ]

andi. ANDs with (48)0 || UI (Power ISA, Book I, "AND Immediate"), so bits
16..63 of the result are zero: the result is already its own sign extension
and the extsw. recomputes the CR0 that andi. just recorded.  It becomes

    andi.  r0,rA,UI
    bc

The register form keeps its extsw.: the and. of two registers whose upper
words are not defined for Word32 values (kPPC_LoadWordU32 is lwz, the
bitwise ops are 64-bit) can be non-zero above bit 31 with a zero low word,
and the extsw. is what re-derives CR0 from the low word there.

The instruction is only ever selected with an equality continuation, so the
LT/GT bits -- the only thing the extsw. could change for the immediate form
-- are never read.  Checked in the selector and the code generator: the
single emission site is VisitWordCompareZero in instruction-selector-ppc.cc,
for a value that is a Word32BitwiseAnd (VisitWordCompare with kPPC_Tst32 and
kInt16Imm_Unsigned, so the immediate is 0..0xffff).  VisitWordCompareZero's
callers in instruction-selector.cc are VisitBranch (ForBranch kNotEqual),
VisitDeoptimizeIf (kEqual or kNotEqual), VisitSelect (kNotEqual) and
VisitTrapIf (kEqual or kNotEqual); ConsumeEqualZero only negates between
those two, and no OverwriteAndNegateIfEqual runs on this path.  In the code
generator FlagsConditionToCondition therefore yields eq or ne, and
AssembleArchBranch, AssembleArchDeoptBranch, AssembleArchTrap and
AssembleArchBoolean (isel on eq/ne) consume only CR0[EQ] for those.

Verified on POWER9 by executing andi. with UI=0xffff on all-ones, on
0xffffffffffff0000 and on 0x8000000080000000: results 0xffff, 0, 0 with CR0
= GT, EQ, EQ, and extsw of each result is the identity.

One instruction fewer on every immediate bit test, which includes the Smi
tag check (Word32And(x, 1)) and bitfield tests on Map and feedback words.
No benchmark was run; this is a pure dead-instruction removal.

Valid for both pools: andi. is base ISA.  Nothing else in the file changes
and there is no ordering dependency on the other patches in this series.

--- a/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/code-generator-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/code-generator-ppc.cc
@@ -1725,10 +1725,14 @@
     case kPPC_Tst32:
       if (HasRegisterInput(instr, 1)) {
         __ and_(r0, i.InputRegister(0), i.InputRegister(1), i.OutputRCBit());
+        // The upper words of Word32 inputs are not defined, so CR0 has to be
+        // taken from the sign-extended low word of the result.
+        __ extsw(r0, r0, i.OutputRCBit());
       } else {
+        // andi. clears bits 16..63, so the result is already its own sign
+        // extension and the CR0 it recorded already describes the low word.
         __ andi(r0, i.InputRegister(0), i.InputImmediate(1));
       }
-      __ extsw(r0, r0, i.OutputRCBit());
       DCHECK_EQ(SetRC, i.OutputRCBit());
       break;
     case kPPC_Tst64:
